---
description: Rules for the Go backend and download engine
globs: ["**/*.go", "go.mod", "go.sum"]
alwaysApply: false
---

- Use idiomatic Go with clear package boundaries.
- Keep engine packages free of Wails imports.
- Prefer `net/http` with an explicit `http.Client` and transport configuration.
- Stream response bodies to disk; do not buffer entire files in memory.
- Bound concurrency, buffers, retries, and response sizes.
- Use context cancellation for pause/cancel and timeouts.
- Validate every HTTP range response before writing.
- Never assume `Accept-Ranges` proves range support.
- Fall back to single-stream if valid 206/Content-Range behavior is not confirmed.
- Prevent overlapping writes and stale-resume corruption.
- Put optional Network Access / Tunneling behind a separate package and interface.
- Ordinary downloads must work when tunneling is disabled.
- Add unit and local-server integration tests for failure paths.
- Never disable TLS verification or log credentials.
